<FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" VerticalGap="16px" Class="my-2">
    <FluentText>
        Assigning training is done from the <a href="/manage/training">Training Dashboard</a>,
        using whichever of these fits what you're trying to do.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">By Course</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Pick a course to see everyone currently assigned to it, their status, latest quiz score,
        and due date. From here you can copy a direct link to someone's assignment, or edit a due
        date without re-assigning anything.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Bulk assign</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        From the By Course tab, use <strong>Bulk assign…</strong> to give the selected course to
        several people at once, either <strong>Individually</strong> (pick people from a list) or
        <strong>By Role</strong> (assign to everyone holding a given role in one step). For
        Managers, a by-role assignment only reaches people at their own location, even if others
        elsewhere hold that role too.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">By Person</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Pick a staff member to see every course assigned to them, with the same status/score/due
        date columns. From here you can drill into an individual assignment's timing, how long
        they spent on each section.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Auto-assign rules</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Each course has a switch to have it assigned automatically whenever a new staff member is
        created, so mandatory training doesn't need to be remembered and assigned by hand every
        time someone joins.
    </FluentText>

    <FluentText As="TextTag.H5" Size="TextSize.Size400">Due dates</FluentText>
    <FluentText>
        Due dates are set when assigning (individually or in bulk) and can be changed afterwards
        from the By Course tab. An assignment becomes <strong>Overdue</strong> automatically once
        its due date passes without being completed, nothing needs to be done to mark it that
        way.
    </FluentText>
</FluentStack>
